cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below. Author details are withheld during peer review and will be added on publication."
type: software
title: "Depth and durability of response in patient-derived xenografts: analysis code"
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous (withheld for peer review)"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - patient-derived xenograft
  - tumor growth kinetics
  - durability of response
  - treatment selection
  - preclinical oncology
abstract: >-
  Analysis and figure code for a re-analysis of the Novartis PDX Encyclopedia
  (Gao et al., 2015). The code separates the depth of a tumor's response to
  treatment from its durability (the regrowth rate after the smallest
  volume), compares the two as forecasters of later tumor volume and as
  guides to treatment selection, and examines what governs durability.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Gao
        given-names: Hui
    title: "High-throughput screening using patient-derived tumor xenografts to predict clinical trial drug response"
    journal: "Nature Medicine"
    volume: 21
    start: 1318
    end: 1325
    year: 2015
    doi: "10.1038/nm.3954"
